@page "/library"

<PageTitle>Library — The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<div class="library-page">
    <section class="library-hero">
        <div class="library-kicker">THE SINGULARITY WORKSHOP // KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM</div>
        <h1>Library</h1>
        <p class="library-lead">This is not a blog archive. It is the beginning of a living technical corpus: ideas, experiments, benchmarks, implementation notes, and eventually chapters that can grow without waiting for a new edition of the book.</p>
        <div class="library-signal-row" aria-label="Library status"><span><b>MODE</b> LIVING</span><span><b>FORMAT</b> CHAPTERS + EXPERIMENTS</span><span><b>STATE</b> BUILDING</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="library-grid" aria-label="Library collection">
        <article class="library-card featured"><div class="card-index">01</div><div class="card-type">FOUNDATION // FSM</div><h2>Escaping Update() Spaghetti</h2><p>The beginning of the argument for deterministic state-driven behavior: stop scattering behavior across an application and give execution a home.</p><div class="card-meta"><span>ARTICLE</span><span>FSM_API</span><span>FOUNDATION</span></div></article>
        <article class="library-card"><div class="card-index">02</div><div class="card-type">PATTERN // CONTEXT</div><h2>Applying the FSM Context Pattern to Scaling</h2><p>Context becomes the boundary through which a state machine receives what it needs, keeping behavior composable while the surrounding system grows.</p><div class="card-meta"><span>ARTICLE</span><span>ARCHITECTURE</span></div></article>
        <article class="library-card"><div class="card-index">03</div><div class="card-type">CASE STUDY // MOTION</div><h2>Completing the Motion Trilogy</h2><p>A practical progression from movement logic toward a more disciplined model of states, transitions, ownership, and execution.</p><div class="card-meta"><span>ARTICLE</span><span>UNITY</span></div></article>
        <article class="library-card"><div class="card-index">04</div><div class="card-type">BENCHMARK // EVIDENCE</div><h2>You Don't Have to Take My Word for It</h2><p>Architecture makes a claim. The benchmark makes the claim measurable. Readers can run the FSM_API themselves and inspect the result.</p><div class="card-meta"><span>BENCHMARK</span><span>OPEN SOURCE</span></div></article>
        <article class="library-card"><div class="card-index">05</div><div class="card-type">SYSTEM // WORKSHOP</div><h2>The Grand Finale</h2><p>The technology stops being a collection of isolated demonstrations and starts looking like a system: deterministic execution, reusable components, and a workshop built around making software visible.</p><div class="card-meta"><span>ARTICLE</span><span>WORKSHOP</span></div></article>
        <article class="library-card future-card"><div class="card-index">∞</div><div class="card-type">NEXT // CONTRIBUTOR SPACE</div><h2>Living Chapters</h2><p>Future chapters can carry executable examples, diagrams, experiments, references, revisions, and implementations. The chapter changes because the technology changes.</p><div class="card-meta"><span>PLANNED</span><span>OPEN TO CONTRIBUTORS</span></div></article>
    </section>
    <section class="library-model"><div><div class="library-kicker">THE MODEL</div><h2>Book → Part → Chapter → Experiment</h2><p>A chapter is not merely text. It can become a durable technical object with source, diagrams, runnable demonstrations, benchmarks, references, and a history of revision.</p></div><div class="library-pipeline" aria-label="Living chapter pipeline"><span>IDEA</span><i>→</i><span>CHAPTER</span><i>→</i><span>EXPERIMENT</span><i>→</i><span>IMPLEMENTATION</span><i>→</i><span>REVISION</span></div></section>
    <section class="library-invitation"><div><div class="library-kicker">THE SHELF IS OPEN</div><h2>Eventually, this library should outgrow its author.</h2><p>The Workshop is being built to make technical knowledge inspectable, testable, and reusable. That includes knowledge written by people who were not here at the beginning.</p></div><a class="library-action" href="/about">MEET THE BUILDER <span>↗</span></a></section>
</div>
